WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.828
Every individual alarm is clear. But the system is not safe.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:10.984
Extraction is down. Hot work is planned. Four people are moving toward the gas corridor.

00:00:11.394 --> 00:00:16.893
Compound Zero connects these weak signals before any one device crosses its threshold.

00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:30.683
The replay is deterministic and simulated. Every state is served by the calibrated model API. A fixed seed makes every event, score, timestamp, and receipt reproducible from end to end.

00:00:31.153 --> 00:00:37.813
At T plus nine, fusion raises the first warning. The authored harmful state is still thirteen minutes away.

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:51.720
By T plus eighteen, the score is one hundred, four people are exposed, and every device alarm still reads clear. That eight-minute lead is the window for controlled intervention before the simulated harmful state.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:01:02.274
The evidence graph shows why. A rising gas pattern overlaps an impaired extraction barrier, an active ignition source, and worker exposure.

00:01:02.654 --> 00:01:17.439
No language model writes this risk score. The path is structured, timestamped, and traceable to source receipts. Each edge records its source, time, relationship, and confidence so an operator can challenge the result.

00:01:18.019 --> 00:01:25.966
The safety officer opens the response studio. Holding the hot-work permit projects the replay score from one hundred to seventy-one.

00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:32.617
This is a non-causal dry run. It records a human decision; it does not actuate plant equipment.

00:01:33.127 --> 00:01:43.809
The same case now enters four bounded services: privacy-preserving event metadata, numeric fusion, cited local retrieval, and deterministic permit checks.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:51.324
No raw camera frame is accepted. No biometric identity is needed. Missing evidence remains visible.

00:01:51.754 --> 00:02:06.165
The response plan requires three human roles. Watch the approvals advance in sequence while actuation stays none and execution stays manual. The recommendation remains advisory until the named approvers record their decisions.

00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:15.352
Now the evidence. On the base whole-seed holdout, fusion detects all sixty-five simulated events, with a twelve-minute median lead.

00:02:15.722 --> 00:02:21.809
But the harder test changes the story. Leave-one-scenario-type-out recall falls to eighty percent.

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:37.402
The model misses the unseen process-drift family completely. That failure is why deployment remains behind local calibration and prospective shadow validation. The interface exposes that miss instead of hiding it behind aggregate accuracy.

00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:45.445
The safety case keeps the decision, model version, input receipts, operator action, and limitations together.

00:02:45.785 --> 00:02:54.952
The policy gate is explicit. Advisory notifications may be automatic. Permit holds need a person. Process isolation needs two.

00:02:55.392 --> 00:03:10.126
Legal and standards references are navigation aids, not certification. The prototype also keeps physical alarms and safety-instrumented systems independent. Every exported evidence bundle preserves those boundaries for review.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:21.012
What did we build? Five working operator workspaces, a calibrated risk API, honest robustness evidence, and a human-gated response path.

00:03:21.502 --> 00:03:30.894
Compound Zero does not replace the plant's safety systems or its people. It gives them the missing context, and the time, to act before the alarm.
